Note! If you want to skip step 1 & 2 - use the prefiltered somatic mutations 
provided in the folder input_data/WGS: SNVs.tsv (SNVs for all patients), 
mutations.tsv (SNVs + indels for all patients), and shared_mutations_SNV.rds 
(matrix with number of overlapping SNVs within each patient). Input files needed 
for the NanoSeq analysis are provided in the folder input_data/NanoSeq.

# --- 1. Preprocess from FASTQ

A. Whole-genome sequencing (WGS)
To run the preprocessing the following tools are needed:
bwa (v0.7.17-r1188)
samtools (v1.22.1)
GATK toolkit (v4.1.5.0)
Varscan (v2.3.9)
VEP (v109)

  * Align FASTQ files using bwa mem -M.
  * Identify duplicated reads using MarkDuplicates (GATK toolkit) with default 
    settings.
  * Base quality score recalibration using BaseRecalibrator followed by ApplyBQSR 
    (GATK toolkit), with default settings.
  * Mutation calling using Mutect2 (GATK toolkit) and Varscan with default settings.  
  * Annotate filtered mutation calls from Mutect2 using VEP (mutations marked 
    with PASS in Mutect2 output).

B. Nanorate sequencing (NanoSeq)
Follow the pipeline provided at https://github.com/AlexandrovLab/DupCaller (version 1.2.1). 

# --- 2. Filter somatic mutation (WGS)

* Run the script scripts/analysis/filter.R. You will need text files with unfiltered mutation calls
  for each sample (provided from running step 1) together with metadata (provided) 
  and panel of normals. From this script you get text files of mutations, SNVs and 
  a matrix with overlapping mutations within each patient, used in further analyses.
  
* PON is generated from Germline and LOH calls from Varscan. Variants supported 
  by > 1 read in the blood normal of > 1 patient are included in the PON, thus 
  removed from the filtered somatic calls. 
  
* The expected tsv files needed to run the script:
    sample_code.filtered.onlyPASS.vep.tsv: Filtered (only PASS) and vep annotated output from Mutect2 (Expected rownames: sample_id, chr, pos, ref, alt, tumor_alt_read_depth_r1, tumor_alt_read_depth_r2, tumor_ref_read_depth_r1, tumor_ref_read_depth_r2, normal_alt_read_depth_r1, normal_alt_read_depth_r2, normal_ref_read_depth_r1, normal_ref_read_depth_r2, Consequence, IMPACT, SYMBOL, BIOTYPE, Existing_variation, DISTANCE, SIFT, PolyPhen
    sample_code.filtered.tsv: Raw output from FilterMutectCalls (Expected rownames: sample_id, chr, pos, ref, alt, tumor_alt_read_depth_r1, tumor_alt_read_depth_r2, tumor_ref_read_depth_r1, tumor_ref_read_depth_r2, normal_alt_read_depth_r1, normal_alt_read_depth_r2, normal_ref_read_depth_r1, normal_ref_read_depth_r2)
    sample_code.indel.Somatic: Unfiltered indel output from Varscan (Expected rownames: chrom, position, ref, var, normal_reads1, normal_reads2, normal_var_freq, normal_gt, tumor_reads1, tumor_reads2, tumor_var_freq, tumor_gt, somatic_status, variant_p_value, somatic_p_value, tumor_reads1_plus, tumor_reads1_minus, tumor_reads2_plus, tumor_reads2_minus, normal_reads1_plus, normal_reads1_minus, normal_reads2_plus normal_reads2_minus)
    sample_code.snp.Somatic: Unfiltered snp output from Varscan (Expected rownames: Same as sample_code.indel.Somatic.formated)
    sample_code.indel.Somatic.hc: Filtered (hc) indel output from Varscan (Expected rownames: Same as sample_code.indel.Somatic.formated)
    sample_code.snp.Somatic.hc: Filtered (hc) snp output from Varscan (Expected rownames: Same as sample_code.indel.Somatic.formated)
    
  Note! Indel output from Varscan need to be parsed to match the reference and variant base notation used in Mutect2. 

# --- 3. WGD analysis
* Run the script 'scripts/analysis/WGD.R' to produce the file 'input_data/WGS/WGD.tsv' 
  used in 'scripts/analysis/figure2_figure3_read_data.R'. The result is already provided 
  under 'input_data/WGS/WGD.tsv' and can be used directly in other analyses. 

# --- 4. Signature analysis - SigProfilerAssignment

* To run this analysis, MatrixGenerator (v1.2.25) and SigProfilerAssignment (v0.1.4) 
  are needed. The input files needed to produce the figure are provided and 
  can be used directly. 
* Run the script scripts/analysis/Signatures/matrixgenerator/prepare_input_bootstrap.R
  to produce the input files for MatrixGenerator. 
* Run the script scripts/analysis/Signatures/matrixgenerator/prepare_input_bootstrap.R
* Run the script scripts/analysis/Signatures/sigprofiler/run_SigProfiler_bootstrap.R

# --- 5. Purity, ploidy, and coverage analyses

* Purity: Run the script 'scripts/analysis/PurBayes/run_purbayes.R'. The result 
  is already provided under 'input_data/WGS/purity.tsv' and this file can be used 
  directly in other analyses. 
  
* Coverage: Run samtools idxstats and summarise the totalt read count 
  (chr1-22 + chrX and chr Y) for each sample. The result is already provided under 
  'input_data/WGS/output_idxstats.tsv' and this file can be used directly in 
  other analyses. 

# --- 6. Reproduce figures

* Run the scripts figure1.R, figure2.R, figure3.R to reproduce the main figures 
  of the genomic analyses from the paper. The scripts can be found in det folder
  scripts/main_figures. Note! In figure3.R, the script produces phylogenetic 
  trees for all patients (Supplementary figure 6) and not only the examples 
  shown in Figure 3. 
  
* Run the scripts in the folder scripts/supp_figures to reproduce 
  Supplementary figures 2, 5, 7 and figures in Supplementary Note 1.

# --- 7. Supplementary tables

* Run the script 'scripts/supplementary_tables.R' to reproduce Supplementary 
  tables 1 and 3-7.